.TH "LMM" "1" "Jul 2026" "lmm 1.28.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
lmm-game-detect - Detect Steam games and add them to config


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlmm game detect [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan Steam libraries for known moddable games and optionally add them to games.yaml.

.PP
Prompts for which games to add (e.g. 1,2 or all or none). Each added
game gets a NexusMods source mapping, the symlink link method, and an
empty default profile; edit games.yaml afterwards for anything more
specific, including the NexusMods slug if none was detected.

.PP
Examples:
  lmm game detect


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for detect


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config directory (default: ~/.config/lmm)

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	data directory (default: ~/.local/share/lmm)

.PP
\fB-g\fP, \fB--game\fP=""
	game ID to operate on

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output in JSON format (list, status, search, update, conflicts, verify, mod show, source list)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colored output (NO_COLOR env is also honored)

.PP
\fB--no-hooks\fP[=false]
	disable all hooks

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


